From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LLCOOLT <114613597+LLCOOLT@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] gfx: a graphics API that failed to make a device is passed over

A player's Intel UHD (Ice Lake, a 2020 driver) logged "D3D12CreateDevice
failed with DXGI_ERROR_DRIVER_INTERNAL_ERROR (0x887A0020) - While
initializing adapter" while Dawn listed D3D12's adapters. Dawn dropped that
adapter and handed out the driver's other one, Aurora kept D3D12, and the
driver crashed the process (a read of 0 in igd12umd64) in the next calls:
neither the game nor its launcher ever opened.

- A device-creation failure while a graphics API starts (Dawn's "...CreateDevice
  failed" warning or error, a device lost while starting) now fails that API's
  start: the next API in the order is tried (Vulkan, then D3D11 on Windows).
  Such an API is taken again only as the last resort, once every other one
  failed too, before Null.
- A failed start lets go of its device, adapter and surface. A device-request
  or surface failure left g_adapter set, and the next API's start skipped its
  own adapter request (the loop runs while !g_adapter): the failed adapter was
  used again under the next API's name.
- Each API is tried once (the desired one was tried twice: alone, then again in
  the order).
- AuroraConfig.backendAttemptCallback: called before each API is tried; false
  passes it over (an application notes which one is starting, so one that ended
  the process while it started is passed over at the next start).
- $AURORA_FAIL_BACKEND=d3d12[,vulkan,...] (tests): that API's start reports a
  device-creation failure.
- No graphics device at all: the message box says to update the graphics driver.
---
diff --git a/include/aurora/aurora.h b/include/aurora/aurora.h
index 7a97618..41965e9 100644
--- a/include/aurora/aurora.h
+++ b/include/aurora/aurora.h
@@ -130,6 +130,13 @@ typedef struct {
    * not pause the app. Not for desktops where a hidden window gets no surface (Wayland).
    */
   bool offscreen;
+
+  /*
+   * Called before each graphics API is tried at start (the desired one, then the preferred order); false passes it
+   * over. An application can note which one is starting, so that a driver that ends the process while it starts
+   * is passed over at the next start. NULL: every one is tried.
+   */
+  bool (*backendAttemptCallback)(AuroraBackend backend);
 } AuroraConfig;
 
 typedef struct {
